        "content": "<p>What is the best way to programmatically build a <code>do</code> sequence in Lean v4.28.0?</p>\n<p>I found this function</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkDoSeq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">doElems</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Array</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Syntax</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Syntax</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">mkNode</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`Lean.Parser.Term.doSeqIndent</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">mkNullNode</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">doElems</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">doElem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkNullNode</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">doElem</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkNullNode</span><span class=\"o\">]]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>in <code>Lean.Elab.Term.Do.Legacy</code>, but it generated </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">elaboration</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">function</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`Lean.Parser.Term.doSeqIndent</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">has</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">been</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">implemented</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">failed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pretty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">print</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">term</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">use</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">'</span><span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pp</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">rawOnError</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">raw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">representation</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 618034765,
        "sender_full_name": "Leni Aniva",
        "timestamp": 1787355714
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I solved it. This was because the do sequence generated by <code>mkDoSeq</code> has to be prefixed with <code>do</code> to become a proper <code>Term</code>.</p>",
        "id": 618042158,
        "sender_full_name": "Leni Aniva",
